window.docContents[17].resolve({"/rules/RG1007/#RG1007-fix":{"contents":"1. Move the quantified parameters into the predicate: replace theorem c (n : Nat) : ExecutableContract (f n) (fun v => v = n) by theorem c : ExecutableContract f (fun g => ∀ n, g n = n).2. Name the computable, safe, non-partial definition that callers use; route callers through c.run.3. Universe-polymorphic implementations are supported; explicit universe instantiation is recorded.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG1007: Executable contracts require supported closed evidence","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/RG1007/#RG1007-fix"},"/rules/RG4004/#RG4004-fix":{"contents":"1. Remove the marker from an example that is an ordinary kernel proof; it is then checked as a positive example.2. For a genuine teaching example, keep the native_decide proof and import only the module that provides it (for example import Init).\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG4004: Teaching examples require authenticated compiler classification","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/RG4004/#RG4004-fix"},"/rules/RG5003/#RG5003-fix":{"contents":"1. Add # Intent with the requirement in your own words, derived from the source mathematics or program specification, not from the Lean statement.2. Prefer a level-one heading; a top-level Verso docstring header must be #.\n\n","context":"Regula rule reference\u0009Rule index\u0009RG5003: Registered public material declarations require an Intent section","header":"How to fix it","id":"/rules/RG5003/#RG5003-fix"}});